-- title:
--   Round six: the parameter map is admissible for all large n
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a round-six parameter record satisfying `Prm.Ok`. For an input length $n$ the round-six parameter map sets $b = \lg n$, $b' = b^{1+x}$, $p = 6b'$, $L$ minimal with $4n \le 2^L b'$, $T = 2^L$, $d = \lfloor b^{\varepsilon} \rfloor$, $\ell = \lceil L/d \rceil$, $\alpha^2 = \lfloor p/(48d) \rfloor$ and the bit volume $V = Tp$.
--
--   Then there is $n_1$ such that for every $n \ge n_1$ all the size facts collected in `Good P n` hold (among them $24n \le V \le 48n$, the bands $b^{\varepsilon}/2 \le d \le b^{\varepsilon}$, $\ell \le 4 b^{1-\varepsilon}$ and positivity of all parameters):
--
--   $$\exists n_1,\ \forall n \ge n_1,\ \mathrm{Good}(P, n).$$
--
--   In Lean:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.params6_ok (P : Prm) (hP : P.Ok) : ∃ n₁ : ℕ, ∀ n, n₁ ≤ n → Good P n
--   ```
